    → Proxy: checked exception → COMMIT → EMI = PROCESSED but payment FAILED!
    FIX: @Transactional(rollbackFor = Exception.class) → rolls back on ALL exceptions

  PITFALL 2: SELF-INVOCATION → NO PROXY!
    void processAll() {
        this.processOne(emiId);  // ← calls real object, NOT proxy
    }
    @Transactional void processOne(...) { } // IGNORED!
    FIX: Extract processOne() to a SEPARATE @Service bean → call goes through proxy

  PITFALL 3: PRIVATE METHOD → CGLIB CAN'T OVERRIDE!
    @Transactional private void process() { } // SILENTLY IGNORED
    FIX: Make method PUBLIC (or at least package-private)

  PITFALL 4: SWALLOWED EXCEPTION → PROXY SEES SUCCESS!
    @Transactional void process() {
        try { throw new RuntimeException(); }
        catch (Exception e) { log.error(e); } // caught, not re-thrown
    }
    → Proxy: method returned normally → COMMIT!
    FIX: Re-throw OR TransactionAspectSupport.currentTransactionStatus().setRollbackOnly()

  ═══ PROXY FLOW REMINDER ═══
  Caller → PROXY → real method → PROXY decides commit/rollback based on:
    ├─ RuntimeException/Error → ROLLBACK (Recommended) 
    ├─ CheckedException → COMMIT (Avoid) (unless rollbackFor)
    ├─ Normal return → COMMIT (Recommended) 
    └─ Self-invocation → PROXY NOT INVOLVED → no TX!
